# React 19 + TypeScript

## Defaults

- Functional components only.
- Prefer **named exports** for reusable components; default export is fine for `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx`.
- Colocate types next to components; export props types when reused.
- Avoid `any`. Use `unknown` + narrowing at boundaries.

## Server vs Client

| Need | Placement |
| --- | --- |
| Static/marketing markup, metadata, data fetch | Server Component |
| `useState`, `useEffect`, events, Framer Motion | Client Component (`"use client"` at file top) |
| Shared presentational UI with no hooks | Server Component (or shared without the directive) |

Rules:

- `"use client"` is a **module boundary**. Everything it imports becomes part of the client graph — keep boundaries thin.
- Pass serializable props from Server → Client. Do not pass functions, class instances, or non-POJO data across the boundary unless supported.
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default. Use them only for measured perf issues or unstable dep requirements.
- Prefer modern React 19 patterns when they fit: `use()`, Actions, and progressive enhancement for forms.

## Structure

```text
src/
  app/                 # routes only
  components/          # shared UI
  components/ui/       # primitives if needed
  lib/                 # pure helpers, constants
```

- One responsibility per component; extract when a file exceeds ~200 lines or mixes unrelated concerns.
- Keep landing sections composable (`Hero`, `Bottleneck`, `Deliverables`, `Economics`, `Footer`) rather than one monolithic client page when refactoring.

## Accessibility

- Semantic landmarks: `header`, `main`, `section`, `footer`.
- Buttons/links need discernible names; icons need `aria-hidden` or an `aria-label`.
- Do not remove focus styles; ensure accent contrast on dark backgrounds.
- Prefer native elements over `div` + `onClick` for interactive controls.

## Imports

- Use `@/` alias.
- Lucide: named icon imports only (`import { Code2 } from "lucide-react"`). Brand icons may be absent — use inline SVG if needed.
- Do not import entire icon packs or barrel-re-export huge modules into client islands.
